# The `Ssum`-at-`49` table of the certificate (data file)

`ssumTable49L[i][j] = unpack (packedRowAt 49 (mult (cSigs[i]).1)) (mult (cSigs[j]).1)`: the
`k = 49` value of the packed row DP of the `i`-th signature group (as row owner) at the state of
the `j`-th group.  Computed by `Submission/numerics/gen_table49.py`, which reproduces the
kernel-verified `k = 50` table `ssumTableL` exactly and satisfies the `A`-step relation
`T₅₀[m] = T₄₉[m] + Σ_v a_v T₄₉[m-e_v]`.  Its correctness in Lean is established, 16 rows at a
time, in `Submission/CertSsum49Row0 … CertSsum49Row16`.
